[node name="range_forest_background" type="Node3D"]
editor_description = "MOUNTED EDITOR-OWNED RANGE SOURCE. This stable slot instantiates assets/source/range_forest_distinct_background.blend through its exported GLB. The northern blue body carries the accepted smaller plan form, an irregular exposed rock-to-skirt contact and a closed blue saddle connecting it to the inland blue range while staying clear of the highway tunnel portals. The source holds 7,536 separate, selectable low-poly coastal rocks: 5,932 at the main northern massif, 704 at its twice-linear-sized western companion, 600 at the north-shore volcanic plug and 300 along its south-running connector shelf. There are no collision objects in the source: tools/export_world_source.sh bakes the rocks into one mesh per 250m plan cell and derives concave collision from every visible mesh with the -col import hint, so a boulder moved, duplicated or recoloured in Blender needs nothing else done to it. The newest 3,200 rocks fill the main massif's formerly blank front beach band with overlapping talus dense at the massif toe and thinning into scattered waterward stones; the earlier 2,480 complete the other visible beach runs. Their authored exclusion bands preserve the north-coast highway and north town. The plug retains its accepted form, subtly off-centre crown and widened south-running sand shelf with a vertically lowered inland reveal; the full-range Option A recovery remains open. Since 2026-09-17 the blue massif bodies (north, middle, south, western companion, saddle, plug) fade from dark rock at the foot to blue above: distant_massif_toe_dark below 16m, toe_rock below 32m, then toe_rock_blue_1/2/3 below 43m, 54m and 65m, each a quarter step toward distant_massif_blue_green, with each mesh cut along those four level contours so the bands end on clean edges and the surface itself unmoved; reassign faces, move the cut loops or recolour the swatches in Blender. Edit the Blender source, not this wrapper or the GLB, then run tools/export_world_source.sh. The city, bridge, roads, cameras and protected anchors remain outside range edits."

